{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1407104-campaign-diary-a-hell-of-neon-fire","id":1407104,"title":"Campaign Diary: A Hell of Neon Fire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-09T02:02:40-07:00","id":1407104,"title":"Campaign Diary: A Hell of Neon Fire","content":"I'm really not the sort to recap his games online usually. But last night, one of my players made one of the ballsiest plays I have ever seen in an rpg, and managed to pull at least a full Henderson on me. The kind of thing where, at the end of the session, I found myself just going, &quot;...fuck... Fuck... FUCK!!!&quot; over and over. And I just kind of have to share the story for anyone who's interested in hearing it.<br /> <br /> So I'm currently running a DND game. One of my players could not make it last night, and I didn't want to run without her just because the party is in the big dungeon right now. So instead I just asked the other players if they wanted to run some kind of oneshot, just so we can all play something. We floated some ideas and settled on CoD, so we start talking splats. I'm inclined to do a vanilla mortals game, just because that's easy, but one of my players had a loved one die recently, and he wanted to play demon. So we're playing demon because he gets all of the votes.<br /> <br /> A few notes going in. My style is usually to just play loose with lore and mechanics anyway, and the fact that I'm expecting this to just be a oneshot that we're all gonna forget about in a week means I'm really not getting super anal about char gen. Just trying to get some sheets pumped out so we can go. Also note that I am pretty much 100% improvising everything by the seat of my pants. Basically, I probably got a lot of shit wrong while running this game, and didn't really care up until &quot;the big moment&quot; because I didn't really expect to come back to this.<br /> <br /> As the players are doing char gen, they're also just kind of improvising their characters as they go, and one player mentions she's modelling her demonic form after an oni, because she really likes Oni. So that gives kind of a Japanese theme, and then another player points out that her cult that she's taken could be flavored as being a Yakuza clan that works for her. So now the game is set in Japan and centered around the Japanese Mafia. Which... was not in any way, shape, or form even close to what I was thinking about doing before this happened, but I go &quot;Fuck it. Yakuza game with demons in it. Cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> As one final note, I am terrible at improvising names for places and things under normal circumstances and doing so for another culture was just not something I was prepared to do. A bunch of my players and I are fans of the &quot;Yakuza&quot; series of video games, so I borrowed a lot of names from that series, which they got a chuckle out of. Just pointing out because, well, you might recognize them<br /> <br /> Our game opens in the Kabukicho district of Tokyo Japan. It's an entertainment district that, for a long time, was one of Tokyo's premiere red-light districts. In recent years, however, the local government has tried to rebrand the area as a more family friendly entertainment spot. This has proven a horrible idea, as they have passed more restrictive laws shutting down a lot of the businesses that were generating income in the area, and families still aren't super interested in going to a part of town historically associated with the sex trade. All they've really managed is to create an opportunity for criminal groups willing to provide those now illegal services to the clientele who still want them. It is in this seedy part of town where we meet:<br /> <br /> Aikawa Kohaku- A Destoyer Saboteur and the wife of Aikawa Kaneda, patriarch of the Aikawa Family. She first approached Kaneda a long time ago with a simple business proposition: power for favors. Being his wife was merely a cover at first. Over time, the affection between the two became genuine. We open our scene on her husband giving a speech to his lieutenants, riling them up about how &quot;these motherfuckers think they're gonna come and take over our territory, but we're going to show them how wrong they fucking are!&quot; His wife sits quietly and dutifully in the back, saying nothing, but restraining a smirk from spreading across her face. This sort of speech usually prefaces an assault on the god-machine's infrastructure, but today, someone has been moving in on the clan's territory. As the lieutenants clear out of the room, he turns his gaze towards his wife. She gives him a silent, subtle nod in approval. Suddenly, the quiet, dutiful wife leaps from her chair and runs across the office. She tackles him to the ground just in time for a sniper round to blast through the window. In that moment, her instincts are torn between protecting her husband and chasing the sniper. She chooses to guard him and make sure he's alright, and in that split second, the sniper escapes. A criminal rival? Or something else?<br /> <br /> Tetsuya Ibushi- A Psychopomp Inquisitor, playing the role of a hikikomori and hacker. In a dark room with the curtains pulled tight, the only light is that of a computer screen. The only sound is that of a keyboard clicking. Despite never leaving his apartment, he knows everyone important in the city. And more importantly, he knows their secrets. As we open on him, he's messaging contacts, investigating infrastructure, stealing information to trade for favors. Suddenly, a message flashes across the screen. The firewall has prevented an unauthorized access attempt. And then another. And then another. Tetsuya manages to backtrace the ip address, but in the time that he does, they've already made significant progress cracking his firewall. He pulls the plug on his computer. Whatever data he loses from the hard crash is worth not having his security compromised. But he has no idea who it was trying to crack his software. Tetsuya has a lot of criminal clients. He does consistent work for the Aikawa family, and he knows a new family has been moving in on their territory. Is this related? Or has he been made?<br /> <br /> Hikaru- Just Hikaru. Like Cher. A Messenger Tempter, his cover is that of one of the high ranking hosts at the popular host club Stardust. He's beautiful, seductive, and unbelievably gay. But the customers at his club don't need to know that last part. He's also the one who is going to take my game absolutely off the rails at the end of our story. As we open on him, he's working the club as usual, trying to sell expensive drinks and, more importantly, looking for marks to sign contracts. As he's doing his thing, he gets a request. It's from a new client. That's weird. It's weird for a new client to just request a host they've never seen before. Her name is Hibiki. Hibiki and Hikaru. That's cute. It's cute that their names match. Hibiki is cute. And charming. Hikaru likes her. The storyteller is telling him that he likes her. The storyteller is telling him that he's definitely not attracted to her. He's gay. But he has the strangest friend-crush on her. He likes her. He wants her to like him. And as he is considering this, some yakuza burst into the club, demanding to see the owner. Hikaru approaches them and attempts to defuse the situation. Please, just sit down and have a drink on me, while I fetch him. Violence almost breaks out, until...? The head goon rears his fist back, and stops. He composes himself. Hikaru catches him looking at something out of the corner of his eye, but doesn't see what.The yakuza leave, for now. Hikaru returns to Hibiki and tells her that he needs to go tell his boss what happens. She tries to get him to stay, but doesn't argue when he insists. He goes back, explains the deal, and his boss calls the local yakuza family who are supposed to be providing the club with protection. Hikaru returns to Hibiki and provides his services as usual. At the end of the night, he walks her to his car, and she leans into kiss him. He feels compelled to accept this, despite his aforementioned gayness. He makes his willpower roll to not allow her to kiss him. His wits+empathy check lets him see confusion, intrigue, anger, and all manner of emotions in-between flash across her face. He plays the interaction off playfully. &quot;Now now, if I give you a taste now, I don't know that I'll get to see you later.&quot; She gives him a wink before getting in her car and driving away.<br /> <br /> The 3 players meet up and discuss what has happened. There are too many strange happenings around the 3 of them to be simple coincidences. Worst case, their covers are blown. Best case, some other supernatural shit is happening that threatens the lives they've been building for themselves. But this is weird.<br /> <br /> As of right now, it is close to 5 AM where I am right now. I'm probably gonna be up for like... slightly longer because my sleep schedule is screwed right now. But I'm gonna continue the story tomorrow, if it seems like people really wanna hear more. Or if it seems like people don't wanna hear more, but I'm motivated to write more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T17:27:54-07:00","id":1408618,"title":"","content":"So clearly I didn't come back &quot;tomorrow&quot; as promised, but life, as we all know, gets in the way.<br /> <br /> So because I know for a fact that none of my players are on these forums, I will tell you the actual deal behind what is going on. The God-Machine knows, or at least suspects, that there are demons operating out of Kabukicho, and its agents have gotten so far as to narrow down the yakuza connection. But the machine feels that if it acts directly, even as indirectly as sending some unknowing human servants, that'll simply lead to the demons going to ground, maybe dropping their old covers and getting some new ones, and leaving the GM having done all that investigative work for nothing. So it is choosing to act as indirectly as possible. <br /> <br /> Enter one Shinji Tanaka. Born in 1927. Died in 1949. And controlling huge swaths of the Japanese underworld for the past 70 years. Shinji is a ventrue in the Invictus, and his ability to procure illegal items and make bodies disappear make him invaluable to the organization. Over time, he has built up a sort of shadow yakuza within the yakuza: A clan within the clan: his Clan. He has embraced his captain, who in turn has embraced his lieutenants, and they, in turn, have embraced several soldiers to create a vampire yakuza. He's even pulled in vampires from other clans to work under him (Like the Daeva chatting up hosts in Stardust, or the Nosferatu who's trying to hack into Ibushi's files. Shinji is the God-Machine's main pawn in this strategy. Through its agents, it has put the seed in his head that Kabukicho is prime Yakuza real estate, ready for a takeover. He has the strength to muscle in, and controlling the district would mean huge profits for his family.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine's plan is pretty simple. It believes that when the PC's start investigating this rival Yakuza family and start seeing vampires, they will assume that vampire is about as high as this particular conspiracy goes. That is to say, they will conclude that if this was the god-machine, they would be seeing angels, infrastructure, etc. Not vampires. And this will make it more likely that the PC's will be willing to, you know, use their powers, assume their true forms, etc. Because they will feel safe that they haven't blown their covers yet, or at least safer, Also, out of character, the pc's are pretty likely to go &quot;Oh man. Demon Yakuza vs Vampire Yakuza! That's cool as shit!&quot; and accept it at face value.<br /> <br /> So the PC's begin their investigations, and they discover quite a bit (Mostly Ibushi, because gathering information is kind of his thing.) First, Ibushi turns his pc back on and goes on the offensive against the hacker that tried to hack him. He does so freaking well that he manages to download their entire system library before uploading every virus he can think of and blowing the computer to hell (I forget how many successes he got but it was something absurd. Like I think he got enough to crit twice, if not 3 times, because of dice exploding.). It's a mountain of information to sift through, but one thing he does find is that the hacker who tried to break him goes by the handle &quot;Gaichu,&quot; which is a Japanese word best translated as &quot;pest&quot; or &quot;vermin.&quot; Going through it, Ibushi finds references to a lot of words he doesn't recognize (Including OOC. Most of these players are new to CoD) like &quot;Invictus&quot; and &quot;Ordo Dracul.&quot; He mostly understands these as being separate organizations who are at odds with one another, and this &quot;Gaichu&quot; has been playing all sides, hacking them all, stealing their information, and selling it to the others. He also discerns where this computer was physically when the hack was attempted, and Kohaku has her husband send soldiers to blow it to hell. This is the big info that they get, but all are conducting investigations in their own way.<br /> <br /> Aikawa is calling other yakuza bosses in the area &quot;on behalf of her husband&quot; to ask them for information about the family invading their turf. She gathers that this Tanaka is a relative newcomer to the Yakuza scene and that he has exploded up the chain of command in a really short amount of time. Like one minute he's a nobody. They next he's an affiliate chairman with a major clan. For a little misdirection I tell her that it sounds reminiscent of an angel stepping into a cover, or someone making a pact with a demon the way that this is described to her.<br /> <br /> Hikaru asks around Stardust about this Hibiki woman. It turns out she was the regular customer of the number 1 host here, Kazuki, before he suddenly stopped coming to work one day. Apparently, he'd fallen head over heels for her, which the other hosts mocked him for. Then one day he just stopped coming to work. The guys all figure he couldn't handle them bullying him and he just quit, but Hikaru, of course, suspects something else.<br /> <br /> Ibushi, meanwhile, is continuing to hack and gather information. He learned a whole bunch of shit I don't quite remember. I wasn't really planning to come back to this, so I wasn't taking notes. The main thing he got other than the above info was that he found that 10 billion yen recently went missing from the clan to which Tanaka is an affiliate, and that said 10 billion was now in his private account. He managed to trace that money backward and found that amount, more or less, being moved in and out of accounts going back 70 odd years. He notes a pattern of the money transferring between a bunch of accounts all at once before sitting dormant somewhere for about a decade or so before transferring a bunch again, repeat ad nauseum to the present day.<br /> <br /> My dinner just got here, so I'm gonna eat and then hopefully wrap this up tonight after I finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T18:12:49-07:00","id":1415631,"title":"","content":"And?<br /> <br /> Still waiting on the henderson.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}